{title: Take Care of Yourself}
{lyricist: Tanya Pelikhovskaya}
{composer: Sergey Rykov}
{key: Am}
{capo: 4}
{meta: lyricist_url https://www.chitalnya.ru/users/Einsamer2/info.php}

{start_of_verse}
[F]Take care of [Em]yourself, do you [Am]hear?...
[F]No need to wound [G]your heart with [Am]sadness.
[F]Morning coffee, chin [G]a little higher, [Am]
[F]Let your soul and eyes [Em]smile with [Am]gladness.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[C]All shall pass — treasure [Em]every moment,
[F]Keeping only [G(III)]the good in memory. [Am]
[C]Hold no pain, seek for[Em]giveness freely,
[F]Forgiving [G(III)]others' wrongs with mercy. [Am]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Let the negatives go from your thinking,
Being too strict with yourself is not worth it.
In this life only love has true meaning,
Everything else is fleeting and doubtful.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Summing up the day toward the evening,
When the stars start to touch the rooftop,
Wrap yourself in a warm cozy blanket,
Take care of yourself, do you hear?...
{end_of_verse}
